    {
      "type": "caption",
      "id": "txt_0478",
      "reading_order": 542,
      "section": "STRIP CIRCUIT - WATER INLET VALVE WATER INLET VALVE",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 223.6025,
        "t": 61.93799999999999,
        "r": 370.41049999999996,
        "b": 55.09089075630254
      },
      "content": "Figure 2 - Water Inlet Valve Strip Circuit",
      "caption_for": "fig_0051"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0479",
      "reading_order": 543,
      "section": "STRIP CIRCUIT - WATER INLET VALVE WATER INLET VALVE",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 317.375,
        "t": 707.8669,
        "r": 511.2850000000003,
        "b": 698.5572225806452
      },
      "content": "¾ ¾ If outside the range, replace the inlet valve."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0480",
      "reading_order": 544,
      "section": "STRIP CIRCUIT - WATER INLET VALVE WATER INLET VALVE",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 317.375,
        "t": 694.8669,
        "r": 559.6350000000002,
        "b": 666.0390008403361
      },
      "content": "¾ ¾ If an open circuit is detected, check connections and harness continuity between control and inlet valve (see Figure 1). If good, replace the inlet valve.",
      "hyperlink_hint": true
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0481",
      "reading_order": 545,
      "section": "STRIP CIRCUIT - WATER INLET VALVE WATER INLET VALVE",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 309.375,
        "t": 485.6469,
        "r": 456.01500000000004,
        "b": 478.03900084033614
      },
      "content": "Reconnect CN5 to control board."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0482",
      "reading_order": 546,
      "section": "STRIP CIRCUIT - WATER INLET VALVE WATER INLET VALVE",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 309.375,
        "t": 472.6469,
        "r": 559.8549999999998,
        "b": 445.03900084033614
      },
      "content": "Set voltmeter to DC and connect lead black lead to CN5-1 (EV1) and red lead to CN5-2 (IS) on the control board. Plug in dishwasher or reconnect power."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0483",
      "reading_order": 547,
      "section": "STRIP CIRCUIT - WATER INLET VALVE WATER INLET VALVE",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 309.375,
        "t": 439.6469,
        "r": 554.3250000000003,
        "b": 412.03900084033614
      },
      "content": "Start the Service Mode Test and at step-1 measure for 12 VDC out of the control between CN5-1 and CN5-2. (Refer to the Water Inlet Valve Strip Circuit below.)"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig_0052",
      "reading_order": 548,
      "section": "STRIP CIRCUIT - WATER INLET VALVE WATER INLET VALVE",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 302.4611511230469,
        "t": 664.1465072631836,
        "r": 559.213623046875,
        "b": 510.3087158203125
      },
      "image_path": "figures/figure_0052.png",
      "previous_block_id": "txt_0483",
      "next_block_id": "txt_0484",
      "caption_id": "txt_0484",
